{"slug": "honey-mustard-potato-salad", "nyt_id": 1025386, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1025386-honey-mustard-potato-salad", "name": "Honey Mustard Potato Salad", "author": "Eric Kim", "description": "There exist entire worlds between a good potato salad and a bad one. The good ones have good potatoes that have been prioritized and not just boiled to death: perfectly steamed, not too wet on the inside or outside. This clever, lazy method — boiling the potatoes for half their cook time, draining them, then using the residual heat of the pot to steam the spuds until tender, like one does with, say, sushi rice — ensures perfectly creamy, pillowy potatoes, whose fluffy edges are excellent at soaking up a curried dressing, dyed golden with mustard, lightly inspired by those delicious honey-mustard pretzel pieces from the snack aisle. If your curry powder isn’t hot enough for you, then add a dash of cayenne pepper or your favorite fresh chile, finely chopped. Some like it sweet; if that’s you, add a pinch of sugar or another dribble of honey; taste and adjust as you go.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 5, "cook_minutes": 40, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"prep": "PT5M", "cook": "PT40M", "total": "PT45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ½ pounds baby potatoes, scrubbed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "baby potatoes", "preparation": "scrubbed", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 large eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 garlic clove, finely grated", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic clove", "preparation": "finely grated", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon white wine or rice vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "white wine or rice vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon mild or hot curry powder", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "mild or hot curry powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon onion powder or pinch of MSG", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "onion powder or pinch of msg", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "3 tablespoons mild mayonnaise, such as Hellmann’s", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "mild mayonnaise", "preparation": "such as Hellmann’s", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons yellow mustard", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "yellow mustard", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoons honey or maple syrup", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "honey or maple syrup", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Finely chopped chives, for topping", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "finely chopped chives", "preparation": "for topping", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Add the potatoes to a large pot. Cover with cold salted water and bring to a boil over high heat. Add the eggs, then reduce the heat to medium-low and simmer until the potatoes are nearly fork-tender and the eggs are hard-boiled, about 10 minutes. Turn the heat off."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Toss the eggs into a cold sink (so their shells crack), then place in a bowl under cold, running tap water until cool enough to handle, about 1 minute. Drain the potatoes, then return to the pot and cover immediately. Let the potatoes finish cooking in their own steam on the off-but-still-warm burner, 10 to 15 minutes. Transfer the steamed potatoes to a cutting board and let sit until cool enough to handle."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Meanwhile, in a large mixing bowl, whisk the garlic, vinegar, curry powder and onion powder to combine and disperse the spices, then whisk in the mayonnaise, mustard and honey until smooth. Season with salt and pepper."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Cut each potato in half, and in quarters, if very large. Peel then coarsely chop the eggs. Add the warm potatoes and eggs to the dressing and toss gently. Shower with the chives and serve warm, at room temperature or cold. This salad keeps for up to 3 days in the refrigerator, covered."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 179.83333333333334, "protein_g": 4.9, "carbohydrates_g": 23.6, "fat_g": 7.5, "saturated_fat_g": 1.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 3.8, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 64.8, "sodium_mg": 358.6, "fiber_g": 3.0, "sugar_g": 3.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["american"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-lunch-potato-salad-side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["curry-powder", "egg", "fourth-of-july", "honey", "labor-day", "maple-syrup", "memorial-day", "mustard", "new-potato", "party", "quick", "stovetop"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/06/26/multimedia/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/06/26/multimedia/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz-googleFourByThree-v3.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/06/26/multimedia/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/06/26/multimedia/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz/ek-curried-potato-salad-fkgz-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 1145}, "video_url": "https://vp.nyt.com/video/2026/03/24/165211_1_Honey-Mustard-Potato-Salad-yt-vid_wg_480p.mp4", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2024-06-26", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:28:35Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "hot-and-sour-soba-salad", "nyt_id": 1012512, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012512-hot-and-sour-soba-salad", "name": "Hot-and-Sour Soba Salad", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "I find any combination of noodles and hot-and-sour dressing fairly addictive, and none more than these earthy buckwheat noodles. You can make a meal of this salad if you add a little protein in the form of tofu, shredded chicken or shrimp.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "PT15M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 to 2 tablespoons peanut butter (to taste)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "peanut butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false, "quantity_max": 2.0}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 tablespoon soy sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "soy sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons white wine vinegar or seasoned rice wine vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "white wine vinegar or seasoned rice wine vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 to 2 teaspoons hot red pepper oil (to taste)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "hot red pepper oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false, "quantity_max": 2.0}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Pinch of cayenne", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch of cayenne", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 large garlic clove, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic clove", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 teaspoons finely minced fresh ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely minced fresh ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon sesame oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sesame oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ cup vegetable or chicken broth", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "vegetable or chicken broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "½ pound Japanese buckwheat noodles", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "japanese buckwheat noodles", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 cup diced or julienned cucumber", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "diced or julienned cucumber", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "¼ cup chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "¼ cup coarsely chopped walnuts", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "coarsely chopped walnuts", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "Lettuce, baby spinach, radicchio or arugula for serving (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "lettuce", "preparation": "baby spinach, radicchio or arugula for serving (optional)", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the peanut butter for 10 to 20 seconds in a microwave to make it easier to mix. Combine with the soy sauce, vinegar, hot red pepper oil, cayenne, garlic, ginger and salt and pepper. Whisk together. Whisk in the sesame oil, canola oil and broth. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To cook the noodles, bring a large pot of water to a boil, and add salt, if desired, and the noodles. When the water comes back to a boil and bubbles up, add a cup of cold water to the pot. Allow the water to come back to a boil, and add another cup of cold water. Allow the water to come to a boil one more time, and add a third cup of water. When the water comes to a boil again, the noodles should be cooked through. Drain and toss immediately with the dressing (whisk the dressing again first). Add the remaining ingredients, and toss together. Taste, adjust seasonings, and serve over a bed of salad greens if desired."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 271.1666666666667, "protein_g": 8.2, "carbohydrates_g": 32.3, "fat_g": 13.9, "saturated_fat_g": 1.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.5, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 0.6, "sodium_mg": 477.0, "fiber_g": 1.0, "sugar_g": 1.4, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["asian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cucumber", "easy", "microwave", "quick", "walnut", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/03/31/dining/hot-sour-soba-salad/hot-sour-soba-salad-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/03/31/dining/hot-sour-soba-salad/hot-sour-soba-salad-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 110}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-04-29", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:30:37Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
